---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Temp Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Temp Easy - Body Temperature Tracker iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/temp-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Temp Easy?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Temp%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I add family members?</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">On the Family screen, tap <strong>Add a person</strong>, or open the menu (top left) and tap <strong>Add a person</strong>. Enter a name, pick a color and add a birth date. The birth date matters: guidance for babies and children depends on age.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How does Temp Easy decide what counts as a fever?</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">A fever depends on how the temperature was taken. Temp Easy uses the published line for each method, the same at every age: 100.4°F (38.0°C) rectal, ear or forehead; 100.0°F (37.8°C) oral; and 99.0°F (37.2°C) armpit. If a doctor gave you a lower line for someone, you can set it in their profile. It can only be lower, never higher.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">When does Temp Easy say to call a doctor?</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Following guidance from Seattle Children's Hospital, the American Academy of Pediatrics and Mayo Clinic: any fever in a baby under 3 months; 102°F (38.9°C) or higher at 3 to 6 months; 104°F (40°C) or higher from 6 months to 17 years; 103°F (39.4°C) or higher for adults; a fever lasting more than a day under age 2, or more than 3 days from age 2; and very low readings. The Fever guide in the app lists every line and links to its sources.</p><p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mt-2">Temp Easy doesn't diagnose and isn't medical advice. Call your doctor if you're worried, and call emergency services for an emergency.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I log a reading?</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Tap the <strong>New reading</strong> button (top right), type the temperature, then choose the person and how it was taken. You can add symptoms, medicine and notes. Tap the °F or °C button to switch units; your choice is remembered. Tap any reading later to edit or delete it.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I export data for my doctor?</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Open the menu and tap <strong>Export</strong>, or use the menu on a person's sheet. Choose one person or everyone, how far back to go, and a format: a <strong>PDF report</strong> to print or send, or a <strong>CSV</strong> spreadsheet. Both include temperatures, the method, symptoms, medicine and notes. The file is made on your iPhone and goes only where you send it.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How does Apple Health work?</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">In <strong>Settings → Apple Health</strong>, choose which person is you and tap <strong>Continue</strong>. Temp Easy then saves your body temperature readings to Apple Health. Apple Health is your own health record, so only your readings go there. Readings for the rest of your family stay in Temp Easy. Temp Easy never reads your health data.</p><p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mt-2">To turn it off, open the Health app, tap your picture, then <strong>Apps → Temp Easy</strong>.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">I updated from version 1.0. Where are my readings?</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Everything is still there. Each person now has their own readings. Readings that weren't assigned to anyone in 1.0 now belong to a person called <strong>Me</strong> (if you had no family profiles) or <strong>Unassigned</strong>. Rename that person, or tap a reading to move it to someone else.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is my data backed up?</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Your readings are included in your iPhone's iCloud or computer backup, if you use one, so they come back when you restore. Temp Easy itself never sends data anywhere.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
